It didn't kill me, so  I doubt it was dynamite. You wouldn't get
fragments worth anything from a tin can anyway, I don't think.

If I was trying to figure a plausible explanation, I'd figure that it
was a flour explosion or something like. IIRC, flour and sugar and
things like that explode if they are packed together, the air is too
dry, and they build up a static electricity charge.  Over here in the
US there have been entire refineries destroyed by such explosions.

